# Personal LEONARDO config for Parrot -- COPY this to config.local.sh (gitignored) and fill in.
#
#   cp hpc/leonardo/config.local.sh.example hpc/leonardo/config.local.sh
#   # then edit ACCT / paths below
#
# It is sourced automatically by hpc/leonardo/{check_leonardo.sh, pilot.sbatch,
# prewarm_hippunfold.sh, prewarm_templateflow.sh} -- so you set your account and
# paths ONCE here instead of editing every script. An env var of the same name set
# at call time still wins (every line uses the ${VAR:-...} "only if unset" idiom).
#
# This is plain bash; keep it to variable assignments (no side effects).

# BILLING account only -- the --account / saldo value. NOT used to build any path.
ACCT="${ACCT:-<BILLING_ACCOUNT>}"                     # find it with: saldo -b
# STORAGE area -- INDEPENDENT of ACCT (you may bill one allocation but store in another
# account's work area). Set the actual path; it does NOT track $ACCT. ($WORK is ambiguous
# with multiple accounts, so give it explicitly.)
WORKDIR="${WORKDIR:-/leonardo_work/<STORAGE_ACCOUNT>}"
REPO="${REPO:-$HOME/parrot-neuro}"                    # clone location of this repo
SUBJECT="${SUBJECT:-010002}"                          # default subject for the pilot / preflight

# Derived layout -- override only if yours differs:
BIDS="${BIDS:-$WORKDIR/parrot/bids}"                  # staged BIDS dataset on the cluster
OUTPUT_DIR="${OUTPUT_DIR:-$BIDS/derivatives}"         # derivatives (also where the prewarmed caches live)
SIF="${SIF:-$WORKDIR/parrot/parrot_sif}"              # .sif cache; prewarm_*.sh read this too (as SIF_DIR)

# --- cohort array (submit_cohort.sh) -- only override if the defaults are wrong -----
# The A1/A2/B/C/D chunk map + walltimes live IN submit_cohort.sh; these are just the
# knobs most likely to need site-specific tweaking.
# PARTICIPANTS="$BIDS/participants.tsv"               # array is generated from this
# SUBJ_FILE="$WORKDIR/parrot/cohort_subjects.txt"     # generated: array index -> subject label
# Partition / QoS names. dcgp (CPU, 112c, 512-node concurrency) is UNTESTED for this
# account -- if `sinfo` shows different names, set them here.
# BOOST_PART="boost_usr_prod" ; BOOST_QOS="normal"
# DCGP_PART="dcgp_usr_prod"   ; DCGP_QOS="normal"
# ARRAY_THROTTLE="%40"                                # cap concurrent array elements ("" = no cap)
# MAX_SUBMIT="1000"                                   # QOS submit cap (pending+running tasks/user);
#                                                     #   guards `run` from tripping it. Phase the DAG
#                                                     #   (run --chunks ...) when 5*N_subjects exceeds it.

# --- EEG+BOLD optimization (submit_optim.sh / check_optim.sh) -----------------------
# A SEPARATE stage from reconstruction: no .sif container, just a `pixi` env (see
# setup_optim_env.sh) running examples/eeg_bold_fit_cli.py against each subject's
# already-reconstructed derivatives (BIDS/PARTICIPANTS/SUBJ_FILE above are reused).
# OPTIM_OUTPUT_DIR="$WORKDIR/parrot/eeg_bold_fit_res"  # per-subject fit results
# Fit hyperparameters -- defaults mirror examples/eeg_bold_fit_new.py; override any
# of these here, or per-invocation via the same-named env var.
# OPTIM_ATLAS=1000 ; OPTIM_SPACING=2.0 ; OPTIM_LEADFIELD_LABEL=duneuroCGAL
# OPTIM_OPTIMIZE=both
# BOLD loss is a weighted combination of static FC + dFC/FCD (both computed
# from the same simulated trajectory); either weight at 0 recovers a
# single-mode fit.
# OPTIM_BOLD_FC_WEIGHT=0.5 ; OPTIM_BOLD_DFC_WEIGHT=0.5
# OPTIM_NUM_EPOCHS=300 ; OPTIM_BOLD_EVERY=2
# OPTIM_EEG_TASK=eyesclosed ; OPTIM_FMRI_TASK=rest ; OPTIM_LEARNING_RATE=1e-2
# Unset/empty (default) = reuse OPTIM_LEARNING_RATE for the BOLD step too --
# EEG and BOLD each get their own Adam state, so they can also use different
# rates.
# OPTIM_LEARNING_RATE_BOLD=5e-3
# Optional BOLD spectral-shape term (Welch-PSD MSE restricted to the
# 0.01-0.1Hz bandpass) -- 0 (default) = off. fc_vector's time-averaged
# correlation has no sensitivity at all to each signal's own temporal/
# spectral shape; this adds a gradient for it.
# OPTIM_BOLD_PSD_WEIGHT=0.1
# Optional EEG gamma-band term: log(PSD) MSE over 15-40Hz, alongside the
# existing normalized-linear PSD MSE over 1-15Hz -- 0 (default) = off.
# OPTIM_GAMMA_WEIGHT=1.0
# GPU-memory fixes for atlas=1000 + the long default BOLD horizon (t1_bold=
# 320000ms) -- ALREADY THE DEFAULT in optim_cohort.sbatch/submit_optim.sh, so
# you don't need to set these unless overriding. Validated on GPU (2026-07-29):
# atlas=1000 OOMs even on an 80G card WITHOUT both of these (they fix two
# DIFFERENT OOM sites -- the one-time warm-up solve vs. the actual training
# gradient step); WITH both, measured peak was ~31GiB, comfortable under the
# A100's 64G. See train.build_simulators / network.build_network docstrings.
# OPTIM_T1_WARMUP=30000         # ms; short BOLD warm-up, independent of t1_bold
# OPTIM_SOLVER_BLOCK_SIZE=1400  # checkpoints the scan (~1.3-1.7x more compute) AND drives the
#                               # BOLD simulator's streaming HRF convolution block size -- must be
#                               # an exact multiple of the BOLD period in raw steps (tr_ms/dt);
#                               # 1400 = one TR/block, the smallest valid value.
# Early stopping (train.is_loss_stalled) -- stop once every actively-optimized
# loss's trend has stayed flat/increasing for OPTIM_EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE
# consecutive OPTIM_EARLY_STOP_WINDOW-sized checks. Unset/empty (default) =
# off, matching config.BoldFitConfig's own default -- run stays exactly
# OPTIM_NUM_EPOCHS long unless you opt in here.
# OPTIM_EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE=5   # e.g. 5 -- unset = off
# OPTIM_EARLY_STOP_WINDOW=20
# OPTIM_EARLY_STOP_MIN_DELTA=1e-3
# Cohort-array resources -- UNMEASURED defaults; run `submit_optim.sh pilot` FIRST
# and set these from the observed walltime/GPU-idle before `run`-ing the full array.
# OPTIM_CPUS=8 ; OPTIM_MEM=64G ; OPTIM_TIME=08:00:00
# DEBUG_QOS="boost_qos_dbg" ; PILOT_QOS="boost_qos_lprod"

# --- W&B hyperparameter sweep (submit_sweep.sh / sweep_dispatch.sh) -----------------
# `wandb agent` runs on the LOGIN node (compute nodes have no internet -- see
# README.md's "Hyperparameter sweep" section for why); it dispatches each trial
# to a compute node via sbatch --wait + offline training + wandb sync.
WANDB_API_KEY="${WANDB_API_KEY:-<YOUR_WANDB_API_KEY>}"   # https://wandb.ai/authorize
# WANDB_PROJECT="parrot-eeg-bold-sweep"
# WANDB_ENTITY="<your-wandb-entity-or-team>"              # unset = your default entity
# Fixed list of subjects EVERY trial fits (one wandb run per trial, one sampled
# hyperparameter set). Sequential mode (SWEEP_GPUS unset) fits these one at a
# time; parallel mode (SWEEP_GPUS set, below) fits len(SWEEP_GPUS) at once.
# SWEEP_SUBJECTS="010002,010003,010004,010005,010006"
# SWEEP_OUTPUT_ROOT="$WORKDIR/parrot/eeg_bold_fit_sweep_res"
# Non-swept fit hyperparameters (fixed across the whole sweep) -- mirrors the
# OPTIM_* defaults above; only the 7 fields in sweep_eeg_bold.yaml vary per trial.
# SWEEP_ATLAS=1000 ; SWEEP_OPTIMIZE=both ; SWEEP_NUM_EPOCHS=300 ; SWEEP_BOLD_EVERY=2
#
# --- Parallel (whole-node) mode -- see README.md's "Hyperparameter sweep" ->
# "Parallel (whole-node) mode" for the full measured-numbers rationale. Unset
# (default) = sequential, one GPU/subject at a time, boost_qos_lprod (4-day).
# Set to eeg_bold_fit_sweep.py's --gpus value (e.g. all 4 of a Booster node)
# to fit that many subjects SIMULTANEOUSLY per round instead -- MATCH
# SWEEP_SUBJECTS' count to len(SWEEP_GPUS) (e.g. 4 subjects on 4 GPUs) for
# zero idle-GPU billing; a remainder subject count leaves some GPUs idle-but-
# reserved during the last round (correctness is unaffected either way).
# Measured on this project (2026-08): ~6.6h for one subject's full 300-epoch
# fit -> a clean 4-subjects/4-GPUs trial finishes in ~6.6h, comfortably under
# `normal`'s 24h QoS (sweep_dispatch.sh switches SWEEP_QOS's default to
# "normal" automatically once SWEEP_GPUS is set) -- which has no documented
# account-wide GPU cap, unlike boost_qos_lprod's shared 32 (see README.md's
# billing-formula note on why more CPUs/mem here is free once GPUs=4 anyway).
# SWEEP_GPUS="0,1,2,3"
#
# Per-trial SLURM resources -- UNMEASURED for YOUR actual SWEEP_SUBJECTS list;
# run `submit_sweep.sh smoke` first and size these from the observed walltime.
# Defaults already scale with SWEEP_GPUS (8 cores/64G per GPU, 20h wall if
# SWEEP_GPUS is set to stay under `normal`'s 24h cap, else 2 days under
# boost_qos_lprod) -- override only if your measured walltime needs more room.
# SWEEP_CPUS=8 ; SWEEP_MEM=64G ; SWEEP_TIME=2-00:00:00
# SWEEP_QOS="boost_qos_lprod"   # 4-day wall -- NOT "normal" (24h), a sequential trial can exceed it
